      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, hidl.manager dependency on hidl.base is special case, different from what is described here (it is also \"added automatically\" by Soong, but more like a workaround). What is described here is a generic mechanism: if a Java module depends on a Java library (e.g. it has it in `libs` or `static_libs`), and the dependency is an `sdk_library`, then it ought to be in the manifest, but if it\u0027s not, Soong will automatically add it. This mechanism allows to derive many uses-libraries automatically, not having to specify them all in \u003cuses-library\u003e tags in the manifest (which is sometimes hard or impossible due to transitive deps).",
